        "original_id": "bae3d4c5-57e2-5148-822b-2961cdc93b06",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Military Units: 1st Alabama Siege Artillery Regiment (Colored), 6th US Colored Heavy Artillery\n- People: Major Lionel Booth, Nathan Bedford Forrest\n- Events: Battle of Fort Pillow, Fort Pillow massacre\n- Places: Fort Pillow\n\nFacts:\n- On April 12, 1864, the 6th US Colored Heavy Artillery fought at the Battle of Fort Pillow under the leadership of Major Lionel Booth.\n- The 1st Alabama Siege Artillery Regiment (Colored) was also known as the 6th US Colored Heavy Artillery.\n- The Battle of Fort Pillow ended with soldiers under Confederate Major General Nathan Bedford Forrest massacring Union troops who were attempting to surrender, most of them African American soldiers.",
